# Data contents are DVC-tracked, not committed to git.
# Exception: seed/ holds the small hand-built fixture set, which is tracked in git so the
# ground truth stays reviewable in diffs.
*
!.gitignore
!seed/
!seed/**

# synthetic/ is generated and DVC-tracked: the .jsonl splits stay out of git, while the DVC
# pointers and the human-readable card and test-set lock are committed so they are reviewable.
!synthetic/
!synthetic/.gitignore
!synthetic/*.dvc
!synthetic/DATASET_CARD.md
!synthetic/TEST_SET_LOCK.json

# corpus/ is the ingested circulars, derived and DVC-tracked on the same terms: the JSONL stays
# out of git, the pointer and the card are committed.
!corpus/
!corpus/.gitignore
!corpus/*.dvc
!corpus/CORPUS_CARD.md
# the retrieval query set is hand-labelled ground truth: small, and its worth is that it
# stays reviewable in a diff, so it lives in git like the seed fixtures do.
!corpus/retrieval_queries.yaml
